1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
This hackathon adds Meta-powered tools
on top of my existing Music Transformer.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Import a score.
Start with an editable chord sketch.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Your chord sketch opens right away.
Meta starts a background check.

4
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:23,000
Work on harmony without displaying
the original score.

5
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:28,000
Choose instruments, rhythms and drums.
Hear the arrangement take shape.

6
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:49,000
Select the passage
you want to reharmonize.

7
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:54,000
Change up to four chords.
Compare three alternatives.

8
00:00:54,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Muse Spark uses tools to search
for harmonic alternatives.

9
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:07,000
My Music Transformer scores each
against the surrounding chords.

10
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:14,000
Compare and combine the alternatives.
Apply the changes you want to keep.

11
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:19,000
Hear your revised harmony
in the same arrangement.

12
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:42,000
Export a chord chart
or editable MIDI parts.

13
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:47,000
Continue with Harmony, Bass and Drums
in your own DAW.

14
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:51,200
Less setup.
More time to make your music.
